Looking at the code:
```c++
Catalog &DatabaseManager::GetSystemCatalog() {
	D_ASSERT(system);
	return system->GetCatalog();
}
```

it's really strange that your extension crashes here
`system` is initialized as part of the DatabaseManager's construction
and the `catalog` of the AttachedDatabase (`system` here) is initialized as part of the construction as well

So without any reproduction I imagine you're doing something unconventional here

@reporter 

A reproducible example is something we can use to reproduce your issue. See https://stackoverflow.com/help/minimal-reproducible-example.

Also, could you please stop quoting random text in all your messages and put in some effort to write a clear description of your problem including reproducible example? Without that I will be forced to close this issue due to an unnecessary amount of noise. Thanks!

Ok let me start from beginning.

Simple situation. Step by step. Before all, I keep myself as a root for now.

1. I used extension template to create my extension, named it quack2 -> create repo from template ->  clone on my linux pc ->  build it with make, no extra code added.
2. cd to build/release ./duckdv -unsigned

```sql
Install 'extension/quack2/quack2.duckdb_extension';
load 'quack2'; 
select quack2('Jane') as result;
```

┌────────────────┐
│     result     │
│    varchar     │
├────────────────┤
│ Quack2 Jane 🐥 │
└────────────────┘

Which is correlated to instructions

3. pip3 install duckdb
4. Created some python code

```python
import duckdb
import os

con = duckdb.connect(database=':<nick>:', read_only=False, config={'allow_unsigned_extensions': 'true', 'allow_extensions_metadata_mismatch': 'true'})
con.execute(f"Force install 'extension/quack2/quack2.duckdb_extension';")
con.execute(f"LOAD 'quack2';")
```

Imitating what was done in duckdb console.

5. As a result of the previous actions I have an exception

_Failed to load extension: Invalid Input Error: Initialization function "quack2_init" from file "/root/.duckdb/extensions/v1.0.0/linux_amd64_gcc4/quack2.duckdb_extension" threw an exception: "Missing DB manager"_

6. I added some try and catch code in src/quack2_extension.cpp in function DUCKDB_EXTENSION_API void quack2_init(duckdb::DatabaseInstance &db)  , line 72 in the original template code. But that's it

```cpp

DUCKDB_EXTENSION_API void quack2_init(duckdb::DatabaseInstance &db) {
    try{
        duckdb::DuckDB db_wrapper(db);
        printf("after wrapper");
        db_wrapper.LoadExtension<duckdb::Quack2Extension>();
        printf("after load ext");
    }
        catch(const std::exception& e)
        {
                std::cout << "Exception: " << e.what();
        }
}
```

That's it to summarize. Talking about CI tool, as I understand it's actually included as a part of make and executed with it. Corrected me if I am wrong please.

Thx
